<title>UK: EMI says Motown to net 9 mln stg opt profit.</title>
<headline>EMI says Motown to net 9 mln stg opt profit.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>British music firm EMI Group Plc said on Tuesday that its purchase of a 50 percent stake in the Jobete companies will contribute operating profits of some nine million stg in first full year.</p>
<p>EMI earlier said it was paying $132 million in cash for the stake in the Jobete companies, which control the back catalogue of classic Motown soul songs.</p>
<p>The Jobete companies, Jobete Music Co Inc. and Stone Diamond Music Corporation are owned by Motown founder Berry Gordy and his sister Esther Edwards.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4366</p>
